flowchart TB
    accTitle: How Make and Ninja schedule a C++ build
    accDescr: CMake reads CMakeLists.txt and generates either build.ninja for Ninja or a Makefile for Make. The chosen tool can run the two compile jobs in parallel. The link job waits for both object files and produces vector-norm.
    cmake["CMake reads CMakeLists.txt"]
    cmake -->|Ninja generator| ninja["Ninja reads build.ninja"]
    cmake -->|Unix Makefiles generator| make["Make reads Makefile"]
    ninja --> schedule["The chosen tool schedules ready jobs"]
    make --> schedule
    schedule --> main["Compile main.cpp → main.o"]
    schedule --> norm["Compile vector_norm.cpp → vector_norm.o"]
    main --> link["Link both objects → vector-norm"]
    norm --> link

    classDef tool fill:#e5eefb,stroke:#426da2,color:#173453
    classDef compile fill:#eaf7f5,stroke:#28877c,color:#153c37
    classDef result fill:#fff5dd,stroke:#ad7b21,color:#534217
    class ninja,make tool
    class main,norm compile
    class link result
